<%- include('../partials/head', { title: title, pageTitle: pageTitle, purpose: purpose, breadcrumb: 'Security Events' }) %>

<div class="ws-card">
  <form method="get" action="/security/events" class="ws-filters">
    <div>
      <label class="ws-form__label" for="type">Attack type</label>
      <select class="ws-input" id="type" name="type">
        <option value="">All types</option>
        <% for (const type of options.types) { %>
          <option value="<%= type %>" <%= filters.type === type ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= type %></option>
        <% } %>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div>
      <label class="ws-form__label" for="severity">Severity</label>
      <select class="ws-input" id="severity" name="severity">
        <option value="">All severities</option>
        <% for (const severity of options.severities) { %>
          <option value="<%= severity %>" <%= filters.severity === severity ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= severity %></option>
        <% } %>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div>
      <label class="ws-form__label" for="result">Result</label>
      <select class="ws-input" id="result" name="result">
        <option value="">All results</option>
        <% for (const result of options.results) { %>
          <option value="<%= result %>" <%= filters.result === result ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= result %></option>
        <% } %>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div>
      <label class="ws-form__label" for="search">Search</label>
      <input class="ws-input" id="search" name="search" type="search" value="<%= filters.search %>"
             placeholder="endpoint, rule or payload text">
    </div>
    <div class="ws-filters__actions">
      <button class="ws-btn ws-btn--primary" type="submit">Apply</button>
      <a class="ws-btn ws-btn--secondary" href="/security/events">Reset</a>
    </div>
  </form>
</div>

<div class="ws-card">
  <div class="ws-card__title">
    <span>Detected attempts</span>
    <span class="ws-small ws-muted"><%= total %> matching event<%= total === 1 ? '' : 's' %></span>
  </div>

  <% if (rows.length === 0) { %>
    <div class="ws-empty">
      <div class="ws-empty__title">No security events match these filters</div>
      Run an attack in one of the labs, or reset the filters.
    </div>
  <% } else { %>
    <div class="ws-table-scroll">
      <table class="ws-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Timestamp</th><th>Type</th><th>Rule</th><th>Mode</th><th>Severity</th>
            <th class="ws-num">Score</th><th>Result</th><th class="ws-num">HTTP</th>
            <th>User</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Payload</th><th></th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% for (const row of rows) { %>
            <tr>
              <td class="ws-small ws-nowrap"><%= formatTimestamp(row.occurred_at) %></td>
              <td class="ws-small ws-nowrap"><%= row.attack_type %></td>
              <td class="ws-mono ws-small ws-nowrap"><%= row.matched_rule %></td>
              <td class="ws-small"><%= row.security_mode %></td>
              <td><%- include('../partials/severityBadge', { severity: row.severity }) %></td>
              <td class="ws-num"><%= row.risk_score %></td>
              <td>
                <%- include('../partials/resultBadge', { result: row.result }) %>
                <% if (row.outcome_basis === 'RESIDUAL_RISK') { %>
                  <span class="ws-badge ws-badge--medium ws-badge--no-dot" title="The residual-risk model skipped the SAFE controls for this attempt.">residual risk</span>
                <% } %>
              </td>
              <td class="ws-num"><%= row.status_code %></td>
              <td class="ws-small ws-nowrap"><%= row.user_email || '—' %></td>
              <td class="ws-mono ws-small ws-nowrap"><%= row.endpoint %></td>
              <td class="ws-mono ws-small">
                <% if (row.payload) { %>
                  <span class="ws-table__truncate" title="<%= row.payload %>"><%= row.payload %></span>
                <% } else { %>
                  <span class="ws-muted">—</span>
                <% } %>
              </td>
              <td class="ws-table__row-link">
                <a class="ws-btn--link" href="/forensics/<%= row.event_uuid %>" title="<%= row.event_uuid %>">Investigate</a>
              </td>
            </tr>
          <% } %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <%- include('../partials/pager', { rows: rows, total: total, page: page, pages: pages, filters: filters }) %>
  <% } %>
</div>

<div class="ws-card">
  <div class="ws-card__title">Why the result column is not random</div>
  <p class="ws-mb-3">
    The result is a consequence of the <strong>mode</strong> and the <strong>input</strong>, not a coin flip: one payload
    can end up BLOCKED while another ends up NEUTRALIZED in SAFE mode because they fail at different points:
  </p>
  <% if (residualRiskEnabled) { %>
    <div class="ws-banner ws-banner--warning">
      <div class="ws-banner__body">
        The residual-risk model is <strong>on</strong>
        (<code>RESIDUAL_RISK_RATE=<%= residualRiskRate %></code>), so a minority of attempts are decided the other way and
        are marked <span class="ws-badge ws-badge--medium ws-badge--no-dot">residual risk</span>. Those rows record what
        the application really did on that attempt — the controls were skipped, the leak was real. Set
        <code>RESIDUAL_RISK_RATE=0</code> to make the mode decide every result.
      </div>
    </div>
  <% } else { %>
    <p class="ws-mb-3 ws-small ws-muted">
      The residual-risk model is off (<code>RESIDUAL_RISK_RATE=0</code>), so the mode decides every result. Turn it on to
      give the log a minority tail in both directions.
    </p>
  <% } %>
  <div class="ws-table-scroll">
    <table class="ws-table ws-table--compact">
      <thead><tr><th>Result</th><th>Mode</th><th>What actually happened</th><th class="ws-num">HTTP</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="ws-nowrap"><%- include('../partials/resultBadge', { result: 'SUCCESSFUL' }) %></td>
          <td class="ws-small ws-nowrap">VULNERABLE</td>
          <td class="ws-small ws-dim">The flaw ran and the response carried its effect (extra rows, executed markup, a foreign document).</td>
          <td class="ws-num">200</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="ws-nowrap"><%- include('../partials/resultBadge', { result: 'NEUTRALIZED' }) %></td>
          <td class="ws-small ws-nowrap">SAFE</td>
          <td class="ws-small ws-dim">The input reached the parameterized query or the escaped renderer and had no effect.</td>
          <td class="ws-num">200</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="ws-nowrap"><%- include('../partials/resultBadge', { result: 'BLOCKED' }) %></td>
          <td class="ws-small ws-nowrap">SAFE</td>
          <td class="ws-small ws-dim">Refused before it could do anything: validation rejected the input, or the ownership check refused the request.</td>
          <td class="ws-num">400 / 403</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="ws-nowrap"><%- include('../partials/resultBadge', { result: 'DETECTED' }) %></td>
          <td class="ws-small ws-nowrap">either</td>
          <td class="ws-small ws-dim">A rule matched but the outcome could not be determined. No route currently produces this.</td>
          <td class="ws-num">—</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="ws-card">
  <div class="ws-card__title">Risk score model</div>
  <p class="ws-mb-3">
    Every score is a <strong>WebSecLab Educational Risk Score</strong>, not CVSS. Base per attack type
    (SQL injection 90, XSS 80, IDOR 85), +5 when the attack succeeded, +5 for an authenticated actor, −10 when the
    attempt was blocked or neutralized, clamped to 0–100.
  </p>
  <div class="ws-flow">
    <span class="ws-flow__step">≥ 90 CRITICAL</span>
    <span class="ws-flow__step">75–89 HIGH</span>
    <span class="ws-flow__step">50–74 MEDIUM</span>
    <span class="ws-flow__step">&lt; 50 LOW</span>
  </div>
  <p class="ws-card__note">
    Table cells show the first 8 characters of each incident UUID in the payload-free column — the full value is the
    link target of the investigation page.
  </p>
</div>

<details class="ws-card">
  <summary>Detection rules applied (first match wins)</summary>
  <div class="ws-table-scroll">
    <table class="ws-table ws-table--compact">
      <thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Attack type</th><th>What it matches</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <% for (const rule of rules) { %>
          <tr>
            <td class="ws-mono ws-small ws-nowrap"><%= rule.id %></td>
            <td class="ws-small ws-nowrap"><%= rule.attackType %></td>
            <td class="ws-small ws-dim"><%= rule.description %></td>
          </tr>
        <% } %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="ws-card__note">
    Detection is regex-based and therefore evadable by encoding or case tricks. There is deliberately no rule on a bare
    apostrophe, because that would false-positive on legitimate input such as "O'Brien".
  </p>
</details>

<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
